#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:-1
msgid "The MyPaint Brush Engine manual page."
msgstr "Página de manual del motor de pinceles de MyPaint."

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:11
#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:17
msgid "MyPaint Brush Engine"
msgstr "Motor de pinceles de MyPaint"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:11
msgid "Brush Engine"
msgstr "Motor de pinceles"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:21
msgid ".. image:: /images/icons/mypaintbrush.svg"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/icons/mypaintbrush.svg"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:22
msgid ""
"`MyPaint <http://www.mypaint.org>`_ is a free painting program that comes "
"with a lot of specific brushes. Krita can use those brushes for painting "
"using the MyPaint brush engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:24
msgid ""
"You can create new brush presets using the MyPaint brush engine in Krita, "
"but the presets are saved in Krita's .kpp file format, not mypaints .myb "
"format, so you cannot reuse those presets in MyPaint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:27
msgid "Dynamic Inputs"
msgstr "Entradas dinámicas"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:29
msgid ""
"Dynamic Inputs are a way for MyPaint to get information of the external "
"devices as a drawing tablet; for instance the pressure over the drawing "
"tablet, the speed of pencil movement, the pencil tilt .. etc. They are "
"equivalent to :ref:`sensors` in Krita."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:31
msgid "MyPaint has 9 inputs:"
msgstr "MyPaint tiene 9 entradas:"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:34
msgid "Pressure"
msgstr "Presión"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:34
msgid "The pressure handled by a tablet. Typically in the range 0.0 to 1.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:37
msgid "Fine Speed"
msgstr "Velocidad de precisión"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:37
msgid "How quickly the stylus is moving. This can vary quite a lot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:40
msgid "Gross Speed"
msgstr "Velocidad bruta"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:40
msgid "Similar to fine speed but it changes very slowly."
msgstr "Similar a la velocidad de precisión, pero cambia muy lentamente."

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:43
msgid "Random"
msgstr "Aleatoria"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:43
msgid "Fast and random noise, changes with every brush stroke."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:46
#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:240
msgid "Stroke"
msgstr "Trazo"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:46
msgid ""
"This input goes slowly from 0.0 to 1.0 while the stroke is being applied. "
"This is related to \"stroke duration\" and \"stroke holdtime\" settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:49
msgid "Direction"
msgstr "Dirección"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:49
msgid "This input defines the angle of a stroke, in degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:52
msgid "Declination"
msgstr "Declinación"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:52
msgid ""
"This input defines the declination of the stylus tilt. This is the same as "
"tilt-elevation in Krita."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:55
msgid "Ascension"
msgstr "Ascensión"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:55
msgid ""
"Straight pen ascension. When the active tip points to it, it is 0. When the "
"pen turns 90 degrees clockwise is +90. When it turns 90 degrees "
"counterclockwise is -90. This is the same as tilt-direction in Krita."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:58
msgid ""
"This is a user-defined input. It is related to the \"customized input\" "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:59
msgid "Custom"
msgstr "Personalizado"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:62
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "Parámetros"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:65
msgid "Has the following parameters:"
msgstr "Tiene los siguientes parámetros:"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:67
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_basic`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_basic`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:68
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_color`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_color`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:69
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_speed`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_speed`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:70
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_dabs`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_dabs`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:71
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_opacity`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_opacity`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:72
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_tracking`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_tracking`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:73
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_smudge`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_smudge`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:74
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_stroke`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_stroke`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:75
msgid ":ref:`mypaint_custom`"
msgstr ":ref:`mypaint_custom`"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:81
msgid "Basic"
msgstr "Básico"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:84
msgid "Radius"
msgstr "Radio"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:85
msgid ""
"This is to set the radius of the brush. Please note that all of the mypaint "
"radii are logarithmic. For instance, if you are setting the radius of a "
"preset to say, 2.0 then the actual radius of the preset is going to be "
"e^(2.0) which is equal to 7.389. This makes the size of the brush equal to "
"14.78. So, we can say that mypaint_radius = log(actual_radius)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:88
msgid "Hardness"
msgstr "Dureza"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:89
msgid "Hardness defines the sharpness of the brushes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:92
msgid ".. image:: /images/brushes/mypaint/hardness.png"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/brushes/mypaint/hardness.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:94
msgid "Eraser"
msgstr "Borrador"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:95
msgid "If this option is checked the brush will act as an eraser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:98
msgid "Radius by Random"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:99
msgid ""
"This option is used to generate a brush preset whose radii and opacity "
"change randomly during the stroke. This should not be confused with the "
"random dynamic option in the radius setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:102
msgid "Anti Aliasing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:103
msgid ""
"This option is used to smoothen the edges of the brush and remove the "
"jagging effect. Most useful for very small presets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:106
msgid "Elliptical Dab: Angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:107
msgid ""
"Sets the angle of the brush dabs. Gives the best results for brushes with a "
"low ratio and a direction filter, and allows for strokes akin to a "
"calligraphic pen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:110
msgid "Elliptical Dab: Ratio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:111
msgid "This option is used to change the aspect ratio of dab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:114
msgid ".. image:: /images/brushes/mypaint/elliptical_dab_ratio.png"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/brushes/mypaint/elliptical_dab_ratio.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:116
msgid "Direction Filter"
msgstr "Filtro de dirección"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:117
msgid ""
"This option is used to make the dabs adhere to a specific vector direction. "
"In simple words, at times you might find the dabs not following the vector "
"path of your strokes, this setting helps us rectify that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:122
msgid "Color"
msgstr "Color"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:125
msgid "Change color Hue"
msgstr "Cambiar el tinte del color"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:126
msgid ""
"This option is used to shift the hue in a clockwise or anti-clockwise "
"direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:129
msgid "Change color Lightness"
msgstr "Cambiar la claridad del color"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:130
msgid ""
"This option is used to change color luminance using the HSL color model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:133
msgid "Change color Value"
msgstr "Cambiar el valor del color"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:134
msgid ""
"This option is used to change color value (brightness, intensity) in HSV "
"color model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:137
msgid "Change color Saturation HSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:138
msgid "This option is used to change color saturation using HSL color model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:141
msgid "Change color Saturation HSV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:142
msgid "This option is used to change color saturation using HSV color model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:147
msgid "Speed"
msgstr "Velocidad"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:150
msgid "Fine Speed Gamma"
msgstr "Gamma de la velocidad de precisión"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:151
msgid ""
"This option is used to change the reaction of the fine speed input to "
"extreme physical speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:154
msgid "Gross Speed Gamma"
msgstr "Gamma de la velocidad bruta"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:155
msgid ""
"This option is used to change the reaction of gross speed to extreme "
"physical speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:158
msgid "Fine Speed Slowness / Fine Speed Filter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:159
msgid ""
"This option describes how slow the input fine speed is following the real "
"speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:162
msgid "Gross Speed Slowness / Gross Speed Filter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:163
msgid ""
"This option describes how slow the input gross speed is following the real "
"speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:166
msgid "Offset by Speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:167
msgid ""
"This option is used to change the position of dabs based on stroke speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:170
msgid "Offset By Random [Jitter]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:171
msgid ""
"This option adds a random offset to the position where each dab is drawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:176
msgid "Dabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:179
msgid "Dabs per Actual Radius"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:180
msgid ""
"This option describes how many dabs to draw when the pointer moves the "
"distance of the brush radius."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:183
msgid "Dabs per Second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:184
msgid ""
"This option describes how many dabs to draw per second irrespective of any "
"other parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:189
msgid "Opacity"
msgstr "Opacidad"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:192
msgid "Opaque"
msgstr "Opaco"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:193
msgid "Opaque describe the translucency or transparency of mypaint brushes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:196
msgid "Opaque Linearize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:197
msgid ""
"This option lets you correct the nonlinearity introduced by blending "
"multiple dabs on top of each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:200
msgid "Opaque Multiply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:201
msgid "This makes opacity depend on pressure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:206
msgid "Tracking"
msgstr "Seguimiento"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:209
msgid "Slow Tracking"
msgstr "Seguimiento lento"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:210
msgid ""
"Slow pointer tracking speed. Higher values remove jitter in cursor "
"movements. Useful for drawing smooth outlines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:213
msgid "Slow Tracking per Dab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:214
msgid "Similar to above but at a brushdab level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:217
msgid "Tracking Noise"
msgstr "Ruido de seguimiento"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:218
msgid ""
"Add randomness to the mouse pointer. This usually generates many small lines "
"in random directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:223
#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:226
msgid "Smudge"
msgstr "Tiznado"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:227
msgid ""
"This option lets you smudge, by picking a color from the canvas and mixing "
"this with the brush color. The color slowly changes to the color you are "
"painting on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:230
msgid "Smudge Length"
msgstr "Longitud de tiznado"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:231
msgid ""
"This option controls how much the painting color is mixed with the colors "
"from the canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:234
msgid "Smudge Radius logarithmic"
msgstr "Radio de tiznado logarítmico"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:235
msgid ""
"This option modifies the radius of the circle where the color is picked up "
"for smudging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:243
msgid "Stroke Duration logarithmic"
msgstr "Duración del trazo logarítmica"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:244
msgid ""
"This option describes how far you have to move until the stroke input "
"becomes 1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:247
msgid "Stroke Holdtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:248
msgid ""
"This option defines how long the stroke input stays at 1.0. After that it "
"will go back towards 0.0 and then start increasing again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:251
msgid "Stroke Threshold"
msgstr "Umbral del trazo"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:252
msgid ""
"This option defines how much pressure is needed to start the stroke. This "
"affects stroke input only. The MyPaint brush engine does not need any "
"minimum pressure level to start drawing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:257
#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:260
msgid "Custom Input"
msgstr "Entrada personalizada"

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:261
msgid ""
"The idea of this input is that you make this input depend on a mixture of "
"pressure/speed/whatever, and then make other settings depend on this 'custom "
"input' instead of repeating this combination everywhere you need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:264
msgid "Custom Input Slowness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/brushes/brush_engines/mypaint_engine.rst:265
msgid ""
"This option defines how slow the custom input setting actually follows the "
"desired value."
msgstr ""
